-->

## SYNOPSIS

`unicode-tag-stdin`

## DESCRIPTION

unicode-tag-stdin is `unicode-tag`(1) restricted to standard input: it reads no
files and takes no path arguments, so it can run under a tight AppArmor profile
(named `unicode-tag-stdin`) that denies all data-file access. It is the tool the
tool-output neutralizer pipes untrusted text through. The tagging is identical
to `unicode-tag`(1).

## EXIT STATUS

0 on success; 1 on an unreadable standard input or a closed output pipe.

## SEE ALSO

`unicode-tag`(1)
